                    "id": "comp-software-os",
                    "label": "Software, OS & Languages",
                    "content": "## Software, Operating Systems & Languages\n\n### Types of Software\n\n```\nSoftware\n├── System Software\n│   ├── Operating System (Windows, Linux, macOS)\n│   ├── Compiler, Assembler, Interpreter\n│   ├── Device Drivers\n│   └── Utilities (disk defragmenter, antivirus)\n└── Application Software\n    ├── General Purpose (MS Word, Excel, browsers)\n    └── Special Purpose (billing software, statistical packages)\n```\n\n### Operating System (OS)\n\nThe OS manages:\n- **Process Management** — scheduling, multitasking\n- **Memory Management** — allocation, virtual memory\n- **File System** — FAT, NTFS, ext4\n- **I/O Management** — device drivers\n- **Security** — user authentication, permissions\n\nTypes: **Batch, Time-sharing, Real-time, Distributed, Network OS.**\n\n### Language Levels\n\n| Level | Example | Needs translation? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Machine Language | `10110001` | No |\n| Assembly Language | `MOV AX, 1` | Assembler |\n| High-Level Language | C, Python, Java | Compiler/Interpreter |\n\n### Translators\n\n| Translator | Input | Output | Execution |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Compiler** | HLL source | Machine code | After full translation |\n| **Interpreter** | HLL source | Executes line-by-line | During translation |\n| **Assembler** | Assembly | Machine code | After translation |\n\n**Linker** — combines object files.\n**Loader** — loads executable into memory.\n\n### Statistical Packages (ISS-relevant)\n\n- **SAS** — industry standard for statistical analysis\n- **SPSS** — social sciences, survey data\n- **R** — open-source, widely used in government statistics\n- **STATA** — econometrics and panel data\n\n> **ISS tip:** Compiler vs Interpreter distinction is frequently tested. Remember: compiler translates the whole program first; interpreter translates and executes line by line. Python is interpreted; C is compiled."
