                    "id": "comp-networking-security",
                    "label": "Networking & Computer Security",
                    "content": "## Networking & Computer Security\n\n### Types of Networks\n\n| Type | Full Form | Coverage | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **LAN** | Local Area Network | Room / Building | Office network |\n| **MAN** | Metropolitan Area Network | City | City-wide cable TV |\n| **WAN** | Wide Area Network | Country / Globe | Internet |\n| **PAN** | Personal Area Network | Few metres | Bluetooth |\n\n### Internet vs Intranet vs Extranet\n\n- **Internet** — public global network\n- **Intranet** — private internal network (within an organisation)\n- **Extranet** — controlled private network accessible to authorised outsiders\n\n### Network Protocols (key ones)\n\n| Protocol | Layer | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP / HTTPS | Application | Web browsing |\n| FTP | Application | File transfer |\n| SMTP / POP3 / IMAP | Application | Email |\n| TCP | Transport | Reliable connection |\n| IP | Network | Addressing & routing |\n| DNS | Application | Domain → IP resolution |\n\n**IP Address:** IPv4 — 32-bit (e.g. `192.168.1.1`); IPv6 — 128-bit.\n\n### Computer Security Threats\n\n| Threat | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Virus** | Self-replicating program that attaches to files |\n| **Worm** | Self-replicating; spreads over network without host file |\n| **Trojan** | Disguised as legitimate software; opens backdoor |\n| **Spyware** | Secretly collects user data |\n| **Malware** | Umbrella term for all malicious software |\n| **Ransomware** | Encrypts files; demands payment |\n| **Phishing** | Fraudulent emails/sites to steal credentials |\n\n### Security Measures\n\n- **Antivirus** — detects and removes malware\n- **Firewall** — filters incoming/outgoing network traffic (hardware or software)\n- **Encryption** — converts data to unreadable form (e.g. AES, RSA)\n- **Digital Signature** — verifies authenticity using asymmetric cryptography\n- **VPN** — encrypted tunnel over public network\n\n> **ISS tip:** LAN/WAN/MAN differences, virus vs worm vs trojan distinctions, and firewall function are very commonly tested MCQ topics."
