                    "id": "comp-programming-basics",
                    "label": "Programming Fundamentals",
                    "content": "## Programming Fundamentals\n\n### Algorithm & Flowchart\n\n**Algorithm** — step-by-step finite procedure to solve a problem.\nProperties: **Input, Output, Definiteness, Finiteness, Effectiveness.**\n\n**Flowchart symbols:**\n\n| Shape | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Oval | Start / Stop (Terminal) |\n| Rectangle | Process / Instruction |\n| Diamond | Decision (Yes/No) |\n| Parallelogram | Input / Output |\n| Arrow | Flow of control |\n\n---\n\n### Data Types & Variables\n\n| Type | Example values |\n|---|---|\n| Integer | `5`, `-3`, `0` |\n| Float/Real | `3.14`, `-2.7` |\n| Character | `'A'`, `'z'` |\n| Boolean | `True`, `False` |\n| String | `\"Statistics\"` |\n\n**Variable** — named memory location; must be declared before use in typed languages.\n\n---\n\n### Control Structures\n\n**Sequential** — statements execute in order.\n\n**Selection (Conditional):**\n```\nif condition:\n    statement_1\nelse:\n    statement_2\n```\n\n**Iteration (Loops):**\n- `for` loop — known number of iterations\n- `while` loop — condition-based\n- `do-while` — executes at least once\n\n---\n\n### Arrays\n\n- Contiguous memory; same data type; indexed from 0 (most languages)\n- **1D array:** `A[n]` — \\(n\\) elements\n- **2D array:** `A[m][n]` — \\(m \\times n\\) matrix\n- **Row-major** (C) vs **Column-major** (Fortran) storage\n\n---\n\n### Functions & Modules\n\n- **Function** — reusable named block of code; takes parameters, returns value\n- **Recursion** — function calls itself; needs a base case\n- **Module** — file containing related functions/classes\n\n---\n\n### Exception Handling\n\n```\ntry:\n    risky_code()\nexcept ErrorType:\n    handle_error()\nfinally:\n    always_runs()\n```\n\n---\n\n### Database Basics\n\n- **Data** — raw facts\n- **Information** — processed data with meaning\n- **Database** — organised collection of structured data\n- **DBMS** — software to manage databases (MySQL, Oracle, PostgreSQL)\n- **SQL** basics: `SELECT`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `WHERE`, `JOIN`\n- **Primary Key** — unique identifier for a record\n- **Foreign Key** — links two tables\n\n---\n\n### Frontend vs Backend\n\n| | Frontend | Backend |\n|---|---|---|\n| Also called | Client-side | Server-side |\n| Languages | HTML, CSS, JavaScript | Python, Java, PHP, Node.js |\n| Deals with | UI, user interaction | Logic, database, APIs |\n\n> **ISS tip:** Know flowchart symbols, loop types, and the difference between array row-major/column-major. Database concepts (primary key, SQL commands) and frontend vs backend distinction are common MCQ areas."
